      "columns": ["subject", "object"],
      "predicate": "relatedTo",
      "source": {
        "doc": "GV",
        "section": "Predicates",
        "note": "Derived. GV lists each pairing as Subject to Object, and SA-Intro Scenario A calls createEdge with subjectNodeId and objectNodeId. Thus subject and object name the two ends of an edge. The field predicate is relatedTo: GV Predicates defines relatedTo, and epic Q6 (PO decision 5) gives this predicate to each edge that the entry makes."
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "rows",
      "columns": ["*_id"],
      "predicate": "relatedTo",
      "source": {
        "doc": "PRD",
        "section": "FR-DATA-10",
        "note": "The field predicate is relatedTo: PRD FR-DATA-10 names relatedTo, and epic Q6 gives this predicate to each edge that the entry makes."
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "tree",
      "columns": ["children", "items"],
      "predicate": "contains",
      "labelKeys": ["name", "label", "title"],
      "hintDefault": true,
      "source": {
        "doc": "PRD",
        "section": "FR-DATA-10",
        "note": "The field predicate is contains: PRD FR-DATA-10 makes parent to child contains. The field labelKeys comes from epic Q7: the label is the first own string key of name, label and title. The field hintDefault makes this entry the default of each tree hint (STORY-002-09 open question 12)."
      }
    }
